'''Coventry South West''' was a [[United Kingdom constituencies|parliamentary constituency]] in the city of [[Coventry]].  It returned one [[Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)|Member of Parliament]] (MP)  to the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom]].

The constituency was created for the [[February 1974 United Kingdom general election|February 1974 general election]], and abolished for the [[1997 United Kingdom general election|1997 general election]], when it was partially replaced by [[Coventry South (UK Parliament constituency)|Coventry South]].

==Boundaries==
'''1974–1983''': The County Borough of Coventry wards of Cheylesmore, Earlsdon, Westwood, Whoberley, and Woodlands.

'''1983–1997''': The City of Coventry wards of Earlsdon, Wainbody, Westwood, Whoberley, and Woodlands.

