{{Infobox UK constituency main
 | name = Coventry South East
 | type = Borough
 | year = February 1974
 | abolished = 1997
 | previous = [[Coventry South]], [[Coventry East]]
 | elects_howmany = One
 | next = [[Coventry South]], [[Coventry North East]] 
 |region      = England
 |county      = [[West Midlands (county)|West Midlands]]
}}
'''Coventry South East''' was a [[United Kingdom constituencies|parliamentary constituency]] in the city of [[Coventry]].  It returned one [[Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)|Member of Parliament]] (MP)  to the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom]].

The constituency was created for the [[February 1974 United Kingdom general election|February 1974 general election]], and abolished for the [[1997 United Kingdom general election|1997 general election]].

==Boundaries==
'''1974–1983''': The County Borough of Coventry wards of Binley and Willenhall, Godiva, Lower Stoke, and St Michael's.

'''1983–1997''': The City of Coventry wards of Binley and Willenhall, Cheylesmore, Lower Stoke, and St Michael's.

For its entire existence the constituency included Coventry city centre, which had previously been part of [[Coventry South (UK Parliament constituency)|the Coventry South seat]]; in 1997 the city centre was transferred to the re-created Coventry South constituency, with Jim Cunningham being elected as MP.

